// "Look at <slice>, then put any number of them <spill> and the rest on top of
// that library in any order": the look scry, surveil and fateseal share
// [CR#701.22a,701.25a,701.29a]. The slice is mentioned twice, so it is bound
// where it is looked at and read back by identity where some of it is moved
// (`deckmaste_semantics_v2::mentions`); the read's number is the slice's, which
// is its amount's, so "scry 1" reads "that card" and "scry 2" "those cards"
// (`docs/decisions/semantics-v2.md` §7, ruling 2026-10-06). `spillRiders` is
// how the spilled cards land: "in any order" on the bottom of a library
// [CR#401.4], nothing for a graveyard. It replaces the Lean
// `lookAndSort`/`lookAndSortInto` and their computed `lookedCards` window.
(
    name: "lookAndSortSlice",
    kinds: [Instruction],
    params: {"slice": NounPhrase, "spill": ZoneExpr, "spillRiders": MoveRiders},
    body: sequentially([
        lookAt(Param(slice)),
        move(someOf(anyNumber, Param(slice)), wherever, Param(spill), Param(spillRiders)),
        move(theRest(Object), wherever, onTop, [Placement(InOrder(AnyOrder))]),
    ]),
)
